# Conductor: stop a live Duffel token from buying tickets nobody paid for — 2026-08-22
#
# DISPATCH: ./scripts/dispatch.sh git@github.com:Arlencho/olympus-platform.git wave-plans/conductor/2026-08-22-settlement-guard.plan --auto --retries 2
#
# THE RISK, verified in the tree today, not taken from the audit:
#   apps/web/lib/chat-flight-checkout.ts:432 and apps/web/lib/chat-stay-checkout.ts:292
#   post settlement balance. apps/web/components/chat/chat-v2.tsx:542-545 says it outright:
#   while the card flag is off, every cart settles from the Duffel Balance and Olympus
#   absorbs the cost of the booking. Both paths are live and reachable.
#   Today that is harmless because the flights token is sandbox and the Balance was empty.
#   Both facts just changed: the Balance was funded with EUR 500 on 2026-08-20, and #2646
#   swaps the production token to live. After that, a balance-settled flight-only or
#   hotel-only cart buys a REAL ticket that the traveller was never charged for.
#   The only thing standing in the way is NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURE_CHAT_CARD_PAYMENT, which is
#   baked in at build time, so it cannot be flipped in an incident without a redeploy.
#
# WAVE 1 DESIGNS, WAVE 2 BUILDS, WAVE 3 REVIEWS. Wave 1 writes no product code.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

1 | investigate | READ-ONLY ASSESSMENT, no product code, no commits to any app path. Permitted writes are a /tmp worktree only. QUESTION: what is the smallest change that makes it impossible for a flight-only or hotel-only booking to settle from the Duffel Balance while the flights provider is in live mode. Establish the facts first and cite file and line for each. Where is settlement chosen on the client, where is it read on the server, what does the server do today when a request names settlement balance for a non-trip flow, and what does the server already know about which Duffel mode it is in at request time. Note that /api/v1/health reports flights_mode production, so the process has that fact somewhere; find where, and whether the booking handler can reach it cheaply. Then assess at least these shapes and say which is best and why, in terms of what each one still lets through: one, a server-side refusal when the flights token is live and a non-trip cart names balance. Two, deleting the client balance call sites so the card is the only route. Three, making the client refuse to post balance when health reports live mode. Four, leaving it to the existing build-time flag. Judge them on three things only: can it be bypassed by a stale or rolled-back web build, does it fail loudly or silently, and how much of the existing sandbox testing flow does it break. Sandbox testing must keep working, so a guard that refuses balance unconditionally is wrong. Also answer explicitly whether a trip cart, which legitimately settles from Balance today under FEATURE_TRIP_BALANCE_SETTLEMENT, must be exempt, and what the correct status code and traveller-facing message would be for a refusal, reusing existing ratified copy rather than inventing any. Post your assessment as ONE comment on issue 2302 whose first line reads SETTLEMENT GUARD ASSESSMENT, ending with a single named recommendation and the file and line where the change belongs. Do not open a PR. | task/settlement-guard-assess

2 | go-backend | Implement the guard recommended by the assessment posted on issue 2302 whose first line reads SETTLEMENT GUARD ASSESSMENT. Read that comment first and follow its recommendation and its named call site. If you disagree with it after reading the code, say so in the PR body with evidence rather than silently implementing something else. GOAL, in one sentence: with a live flights token, a flight-only or hotel-only booking that asks to settle from the Duffel Balance must be refused, loudly, by the server. HARD CONSTRAINTS. Sandbox must keep working exactly as it does today, so the refusal is conditional on live mode and never unconditional. A trip cart that legitimately settles from Balance must not be affected; check FEATURE_TRIP_BALANCE_SETTLEMENT and the trip flow before you touch anything shared. Do not change any existing status code for any case that is not this refusal, do not touch isRecoverableUserError, and do not touch anything that decides whether a Stripe authorisation is voided or captured. Use ratified copy for the traveller-facing message; if nothing in docs/prd fits, propose the string in the PRD marked PROPOSED pending co-founder sign-off and say so in the PR body rather than inventing it silently. TESTS ARE THE POINT HERE, so write them first: a live-mode flight-only cart naming balance is refused, a live-mode hotel-only cart naming balance is refused, a sandbox-mode cart naming balance still succeeds, and a trip cart naming balance is unaffected in both modes. Prove the refusal tests FAIL before your change by running them against the parent commit in a throwaway worktree, and paste both exit codes captured directly rather than read after a pipe. Run go build, go vet, the Go test suite with race, golangci-lint and make check-api-spec, and paste real exit codes. Open a PR referencing issues 2302 and 2646 with Refs and no closing keyword. Do not merge. | fix/settlement-guard-live-mode

3 | backend-critic | READ-ONLY REVIEW of the wave 2 change on branch fix/settlement-guard-live-mode. You are not a producer: no commits, no push, no gh pr review, no gh pr merge, no labels, no test writing. The harness pushes the branch it checks out, so any commit on a producer ref is a production incident. Permitted writes are a /tmp worktree only. Record the PR head SHA at start and re-check at report; if it moved, report BLOCKED with both SHAs. THE QUESTION THAT MATTERS: with a live flights token, is there ANY remaining path by which a flight-only or hotel-only booking settles from the Duffel Balance. Enumerate the ways a booking can reach the create handler rather than trusting the diff, and include the paths a web build cannot control: a direct API call, a stale or rolled-back web bundle still posting balance, the Hermes messaging path, and any server default that applies when the client names nothing. A guard that only holds when the client cooperates has not closed the risk, because the client is exactly what cannot be trusted here. SECOND: verify sandbox is genuinely unaffected, by test and by reading the condition, since breaking sandbox testing would be a self-inflicted outage. THIRD: verify a trip cart settling from Balance is untouched in both modes. FOURTH: confirm the refusal tests actually fail on the parent commit, reproducing that yourself rather than accepting the claim, and that no test was written to pass trivially. FIFTH: confirm no status code changed outside the new refusal, that isRecoverableUserError is untouched, and that nothing in the diff decides whether a Stripe authorisation is voided or captured. A diff touching no money-path file can still change money behaviour, so follow the behaviour out to the client rather than reading the file list. Post ONE comment on issue 2340 whose first line reads CRITIC SETTLEMENT GUARD, with a verdict of SAFE-TO-MERGE or BLOCK-FIX or BLOCK-ESCALATE, per-finding severity and file and line citations. No vendor names, emails, booking ids or gcloud payloads. | fix/settlement-guard-live-mode
